    {
      "topLeftX": 112,
      "topLeftY": 157,
      "bottomRightX": 400,
      "bottomRightY": 175,
      "content": "We seek to solve this equation by the Ansatz:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 328,
      "topLeftY": 190,
      "bottomRightX": 463,
      "bottomRightY": 225,
      "content": "$$\\psi_{nk}^{(1)} = \\sum_m u_{nk}^{(1)}(\\tau) \\psi_m^a;$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 111,
      "topLeftY": 245,
      "bottomRightX": 675,
      "bottomRightY": 283,
      "content": "i.e., in terms of a development in only the eigenfunctions of the unperturbed atom whose coefficients are undetermined functions of the position vector $\\tau$ of the electron.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 135,
      "topLeftY": 287,
      "bottomRightX": 323,
      "bottomRightY": 304,
      "content": "From (1), one will now have:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 299,
      "topLeftY": 321,
      "bottomRightX": 500,
      "bottomRightY": 391,
      "content": "$$\\begin{aligned} [H^a, \\psi_{nk}^{(1)}] &= \\sum_m u_{nm}^{(1)}(\\tau) [H^a, \\psi_m^a] \\\\ &= \\sum_m u_{nm}^{(1)}(\\tau) W_m^a \\psi_m^a. \\end{aligned}$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 112,
      "topLeftY": 410,
      "bottomRightX": 557,
      "bottomRightY": 428,
      "content": "We develop the given function on the right-hand side in the same way:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 280,
      "topLeftY": 444,
      "bottomRightX": 509,
      "bottomRightY": 478,
      "content": "$$U \\psi_{nk}^0 = \\psi_k^e \\cdot U \\psi_n^a = \\psi_k^e \\sum_m U_{nm} \\psi_m^a;$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 111,
      "topLeftY": 498,
      "bottomRightX": 675,
      "bottomRightY": 534,
      "content": "the coefficients define the matrix that is associated with the potential energy. If we introduce these expressions into the differential equation then we will get:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 180,
      "topLeftY": 551,
      "bottomRightX": 610,
      "bottomRightY": 598,
      "content": "$$\\sum_m \\psi_m^a \\left\\{ u_{nm}^{(1)}(\\tau) W_m^a - \\frac{h^2}{8\\pi^2\\mu} \\Delta u_{nm}^{(1)} - u_{nm}^{(1)} (W_m^a + W^e) \\right\\} = - \\sum_m \\psi_m^a U_{nm} \\psi_k^e.$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 112,
      "topLeftY": 619,
      "bottomRightX": 678,
      "bottomRightY": 683,
      "content": "One obtains a differential equation for $u_{nm}^{(1)}(\\tau)$ from this by equating the coefficients of $\\psi_m^a$; if we multiply it by $-\\frac{8\\pi^2\\mu}{h^2}$ and set, to abbreviate:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 233,
      "topLeftY": 704,
      "bottomRightX": 676,
      "bottomRightY": 745,
      "content": "$$V = \\frac{8\\pi^2\\mu}{h^2} U, \\quad V_{nm} = \\frac{8\\pi^2\\mu}{h^2} U_{nm}, \\tag{6}$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 230,
      "topLeftY": 763,
      "bottomRightX": 676,
      "bottomRightY": 804,
      "content": "$$k_{nm}^2 = \\frac{8\\pi^2\\mu}{h^2} (W_n^a - W_m^a + W^e) = \\frac{8\\pi^2\\mu}{h^2} (h\\nu_{nm}^a + W^e) \\tag{7}$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 112,
      "topLeftY": 824,
      "bottomRightX": 254,
      "bottomRightY": 841,
      "content": "then we will find that:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 329,
      "topLeftY": 842,
      "bottomRightX": 676,
      "bottomRightY": 864,
      "content": "$$\\Delta u_{nm}^{(1)} + k_{nm}^2 u_{nm}^{(1)} = V_{nm} \\psi_k^e. \\tag{8}$$",
